1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,960
Three days in Seoul.

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:03,740
Palaces, markets

3
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:05,560
a city view at sunset

4
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:07,940
and one day that's completely yours.

5
00:00:08,418 --> 00:00:10,268
If this is your first time

6
00:00:10,268 --> 00:00:12,935
this plan keeps each day in one part of

7
00:00:12,935 --> 00:00:13,588
the city

8
00:00:13,588 --> 00:00:16,091
so you spend your time looking around

9
00:00:16,091 --> 00:00:17,398
not changing trains.

10
00:00:17,398 --> 00:00:19,955
I'll show you the route for every day

11
00:00:19,955 --> 00:00:20,826
what to eat

12
00:00:20,826 --> 00:00:24,718
and the small mistakes that trip up first-time visitors.

13
00:00:25,236 --> 00:00:27,776
Let's start with a few things to sort out

14
00:00:27,776 --> 00:00:29,336
before day one.

15
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:30,670
First

16
00:00:30,670 --> 00:00:32,250
check your dates.

17
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:34,970
Gyeongbokgung Palace is closed on Tuesdays

18
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:38,010
and Changdeokgung Palace is closed on Mondays.

19
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:39,750
If your trip falls that way

20
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:41,770
just swap day one and day three.

21
00:00:42,096 --> 00:00:43,156
Second

22
00:00:43,156 --> 00:00:46,116
get a transit card when you arrive.

23
00:00:46,116 --> 00:00:48,616
You tap it on the subway and on buses

24
00:00:48,616 --> 00:00:51,796
and transfers within a short time are discounted.

25
00:00:52,146 --> 00:00:52,606
Third

26
00:00:52,606 --> 00:00:54,674
install Naver Map or KakaoMap.

27
00:00:54,674 --> 00:00:57,546
Google Maps can show you places in Korea

28
00:00:57,546 --> 00:00:59,672
but its directions are limited

29
00:00:59,672 --> 00:01:02,257
so a Korean map app will save you a

30
00:01:02,257 --> 00:01:03,706
lot of guessing.

31
00:01:04,308 --> 00:01:06,568
Flying into Incheon?

32
00:01:06,568 --> 00:01:09,168
The AREX airport train is the simplest way

33
00:01:09,168 --> 00:01:10,908
into central Seoul

34
00:01:10,908 --> 00:01:13,308
and airport buses and taxis are good options

35
00:01:13,308 --> 00:01:16,708
if you have heavy bags or arrive late.

36
00:01:16,708 --> 00:01:19,208
Pick whichever drops you closest to your hotel.

37
00:01:19,566 --> 00:01:21,826
And where should you stay?

38
00:01:21,826 --> 00:01:24,666
Central Seoul works best for this plan.

39
00:01:24,666 --> 00:01:26,566
Around Gwanghwamun, Jongno

40
00:01:26,566 --> 00:01:28,386
City Hall or Myeongdong

41
00:01:28,386 --> 00:01:31,186
every stop is a short subway ride or a

42
00:01:31,186 --> 00:01:31,806
walk away.

43
00:01:32,136 --> 00:01:34,776
Day one is all about old Seoul

44
00:01:34,776 --> 00:01:37,416
and you can do the whole day on foot.

45
00:01:37,842 --> 00:01:40,802
Start early at Gyeongbokgung Palace

46
00:01:40,802 --> 00:01:43,402
the largest of Seoul's royal palaces from the

47
00:01:43,402 --> 00:01:45,022
Joseon dynasty.

48
00:01:45,022 --> 00:01:48,522
Get off at Gyeongbokgung Station on Line 3.

49
00:01:48,522 --> 00:01:50,562
If you arrive around opening time

50
00:01:50,562 --> 00:01:52,922
the big courtyards are much quieter.

51
00:01:53,292 --> 00:01:56,232
The changing of the royal guard at Gwanghwamun

52
00:01:56,232 --> 00:01:59,212
Gate usually happens at ten in the morning and

53
00:01:59,212 --> 00:02:00,872
two in the afternoon.

54
00:02:00,872 --> 00:02:02,612
And here's a fun one:

55
00:02:02,612 --> 00:02:04,072
if you wear hanbok

56
00:02:04,072 --> 00:02:05,772
the traditional dress

57
00:02:05,772 --> 00:02:08,152
entry to the palaces is free.

58
00:02:08,152 --> 00:02:10,372
There are rental shops near the station.

59
00:02:11,046 --> 00:02:13,466
Give the palace about two hours.

60
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:15,886
Then walk east to Anguk and the hanok lanes

61
00:02:15,886 --> 00:02:17,046
of Bukchon.

62
00:02:17,046 --> 00:02:18,286
These are real homes

63
00:02:18,286 --> 00:02:21,606
so keep your voice down and stay out of doorways.

64
00:02:21,606 --> 00:02:23,666
Some parts of Bukchon now have visiting hours

65
00:02:23,666 --> 00:02:24,806
for tourists

66
00:02:24,806 --> 00:02:26,526
so check the signs as you go.

67
00:02:27,048 --> 00:02:29,548
When your feet need a rest

68
00:02:29,548 --> 00:02:31,428
Anguk is full of cafes

69
00:02:31,428 --> 00:02:34,268
and some are inside old hanok houses with

70
00:02:34,268 --> 00:02:37,148
wooden beams and little courtyards.

71
00:02:37,148 --> 00:02:38,008
Order at the counter

72
00:02:38,008 --> 00:02:40,808
and it's normal to sit as long as you like.

73
00:02:41,346 --> 00:02:42,666
In the afternoon

74
00:02:42,666 --> 00:02:45,246
head a few minutes south to Insadong.

75
00:02:45,246 --> 00:02:47,686
The main street and its side alleys are full

76
00:02:47,686 --> 00:02:49,526
of traditional crafts

77
00:02:49,526 --> 00:02:51,906
tea houses and small galleries.

78
00:02:51,906 --> 00:02:54,226
It's a good place for small souvenirs

79
00:02:54,226 --> 00:02:55,706
like hanji paper goods.

80
00:02:56,364 --> 00:02:59,709
If you want a quiet moment before dinner

81
00:02:59,709 --> 00:03:03,723
step into one of Insadong's traditional tea houses.

82
00:03:03,723 --> 00:03:06,934
Try a herbal tea like jujube or citron

83
00:03:06,934 --> 00:03:10,244
and enjoy a slower side of the city.

84
00:03:10,878 --> 00:03:14,818
Finish with an evening walk along Cheonggyecheon

85
00:03:14,818 --> 00:03:17,518
the stream that runs below street level from

86
00:03:17,518 --> 00:03:19,098
Cheonggye Plaza.

87
00:03:19,098 --> 00:03:20,818
It's lit up after dark

88
00:03:20,818 --> 00:03:21,818
it's free

89
00:03:21,818 --> 00:03:23,938
and it's an easy way to end a long

90
00:03:23,938 --> 00:03:24,878
first day.

91
00:03:25,392 --> 00:03:28,712
Day two is for food

92
00:03:28,712 --> 00:03:31,592
shopping and the best view of the city.

93
00:03:32,346 --> 00:03:33,966
Start at Gwangjang Market

94
00:03:33,966 --> 00:03:36,213
near Jongno 5-ga Station on Line 1.

95
00:03:36,213 --> 00:03:39,140
It's one of Seoul's oldest markets and a great

96
00:03:39,140 --> 00:03:41,544
place for breakfast or an early lunch.

97
00:03:41,544 --> 00:03:42,851
Look for bindaetteok

98
00:03:42,851 --> 00:03:46,143
a crispy mung bean pancake fried right at the stall

99
00:03:46,143 --> 00:03:47,241
and mayak gimbap

100
00:03:47,241 --> 00:03:50,220
little rice rolls that are hard to stop eating.

101
00:03:50,220 --> 00:03:52,506
Bring some cash for the stalls.

102
00:03:53,052 --> 00:03:57,652
Then take the subway to Myeongdong on Line 4.

103
00:03:57,652 --> 00:04:01,092
It's packed with cosmetics shops and fashion stores

104
00:04:01,092 --> 00:04:04,872
and from late afternoon the street food stalls open.

105
00:04:04,872 --> 00:04:08,152
Many shops offer tax refunds for visitors

106
00:04:08,152 --> 00:04:10,852
so bring your passport when you go shopping.

107
00:04:11,406 --> 00:04:13,786
From late afternoon

108
00:04:13,786 --> 00:04:17,226
Myeongdong's main streets fill with food stalls.

109
00:04:17,226 --> 00:04:18,386
Grilled skewers

110
00:04:18,386 --> 00:04:19,346
egg bread

111
00:04:19,346 --> 00:04:21,786
sweet pancakes called hotteok.

112
00:04:21,786 --> 00:04:23,406
Most stalls take cards now

113
00:04:23,406 --> 00:04:26,106
but keep a little cash just in case

114
00:04:26,106 --> 00:04:28,226
and look for the price on the sign before

115
00:04:28,226 --> 00:04:28,966
you order.

116
00:04:29,424 --> 00:04:31,185
As the sun goes down

117
00:04:31,185 --> 00:04:33,663
go up Namsan to N Seoul Tower.

118
00:04:33,663 --> 00:04:37,316
From Myeongdong you can walk to the cable car

119
00:04:37,316 --> 00:04:39,794
or take a bus up the mountain.

120
00:04:39,794 --> 00:04:42,272
The view is best around sunset.

121
00:04:42,272 --> 00:04:45,599
Cable car and observatory times change with

122
00:04:45,599 --> 00:04:46,512
the season

123
00:04:46,512 --> 00:04:48,964
so check them that morning.

124
00:04:49,674 --> 00:04:51,874
Day three is yours.

125
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:54,334
Each of these options fills about half a day

126
00:04:54,334 --> 00:04:55,274
so pick two.

127
00:04:55,572 --> 00:04:57,752
Want more history?

128
00:04:57,752 --> 00:05:01,132
Visit Changdeokgung Palace and its Secret Garden.

129
00:05:01,132 --> 00:05:03,312
The garden can only be seen on a guided

130
00:05:03,312 --> 00:05:05,552
tour with its own ticket

131
00:05:05,552 --> 00:05:07,132
and places are limited

132
00:05:07,132 --> 00:05:08,152
so book ahead.

133
00:05:08,574 --> 00:05:11,234
Into design and shopping?

134
00:05:11,234 --> 00:05:12,834
Go to Dongdaemun Design Plaza

135
00:05:12,834 --> 00:05:15,554
and the fashion malls around Dongdaemun that

136
00:05:15,554 --> 00:05:16,714
stay open late.

137
00:05:17,424 --> 00:05:20,044
Want to slow down like a local?

138
00:05:20,044 --> 00:05:22,344
Spend the afternoon in a Han River park

139
00:05:22,344 --> 00:05:23,784
like Yeouido.

140
00:05:23,784 --> 00:05:25,124
People picnic

141
00:05:25,124 --> 00:05:28,024
cycle and order fried chicken to the riverbank.

142
00:05:28,024 --> 00:05:29,104
Renting a bike is easy

143
00:05:29,104 --> 00:05:31,684
and there's always a convenience store nearby.

144
00:05:32,178 --> 00:05:34,504
Or relax properly at a jjimjilbang

145
00:05:34,504 --> 00:05:35,777
a Korean bathhouse.

146
00:05:35,777 --> 00:05:38,602
It's one of the most local things you can

147
00:05:38,602 --> 00:05:39,488
do in Seoul.

148
00:05:39,488 --> 00:05:42,778
Just read up on the etiquette before you go.

149
00:05:43,332 --> 00:05:46,772
And if you have more than three days

150
00:05:46,772 --> 00:05:48,772
explore neighbourhoods like Seongsu

151
00:05:48,772 --> 00:05:50,712
Hongdae or Itaewon

152
00:05:50,712 --> 00:05:52,912
or take a day trip out of the city

153
00:05:52,912 --> 00:05:55,052
like Suwon's Hwaseong Fortress

154
00:05:55,052 --> 00:05:56,772
an easy train ride away.

155
00:05:57,198 --> 00:06:00,718
Almost everything in this plan is on the subway.

156
00:06:00,718 --> 00:06:02,698
Tap your card in and out at the gates

157
00:06:02,698 --> 00:06:04,518
and use the same card on buses.

158
00:06:05,064 --> 00:06:08,584
Seoul's subway is easy for visitors.

159
00:06:08,584 --> 00:06:11,064
Lines have numbers and colours

160
00:06:11,064 --> 00:06:12,624
station names are in English

161
00:06:12,624 --> 00:06:15,224
and announcements are in English too.

162
00:06:15,224 --> 00:06:16,744
When you change lines

163
00:06:16,744 --> 00:06:19,164
just follow the colour of the line you want.

164
00:06:19,722 --> 00:06:23,464
Taxis are easy to find and fair for short trips.

165
00:06:23,464 --> 00:06:25,177
With the Kakao T app

166
00:06:25,177 --> 00:06:28,902
you can book one without speaking any Korean.

167
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:30,283
Before you go

168
00:06:30,283 --> 00:06:33,165
here are four small mistakes that catch a lot

169
00:06:33,165 --> 00:06:34,880
of first-time visitors.

170
00:06:35,598 --> 00:06:35,946
One.

171
00:06:35,946 --> 00:06:37,452
Palaces on a weekend.

172
00:06:37,452 --> 00:06:41,277
Most sights are busiest on weekends and public holidays

173
00:06:41,277 --> 00:06:44,348
so do the palaces on a weekday if you can.

174
00:06:44,348 --> 00:06:44,696
Two.

175
00:06:44,696 --> 00:06:46,376
Lunch after two o'clock.

176
00:06:46,376 --> 00:06:49,273
Many restaurants close for a break in the

177
00:06:49,273 --> 00:06:50,954
middle of the afternoon

178
00:06:50,954 --> 00:06:52,344
so eat lunch early.

179
00:06:52,344 --> 00:06:52,808
Three.

180
00:06:52,808 --> 00:06:54,430
No cash at the market.

181
00:06:54,430 --> 00:06:56,401
Cards work almost everywhere

182
00:06:56,401 --> 00:06:59,356
but carry a little cash for market stalls.

183
00:06:59,356 --> 00:07:00,051
And four.

184
00:07:00,051 --> 00:07:01,905
Trusting old opening hours.

185
00:07:01,905 --> 00:07:03,992
Hours and closing days change

186
00:07:03,992 --> 00:07:06,657
so check each place on a map app the

187
00:07:06,657 --> 00:07:08,058
morning you go.

188
00:07:08,448 --> 00:07:11,348
And one bonus tip.

189
00:07:11,348 --> 00:07:14,388
Convenience stores are your best friend in Seoul.

190
00:07:14,388 --> 00:07:16,768
They're on almost every corner

191
00:07:16,768 --> 00:07:18,168
many are open around the clock

192
00:07:18,168 --> 00:07:20,448
and you can buy water

193
00:07:20,448 --> 00:07:21,588
snacks and a quick meal

194
00:07:21,588 --> 00:07:24,308
and top up your transit card with cash.

195
00:07:24,666 --> 00:07:27,766
A few questions people often ask.

196
00:07:27,766 --> 00:07:29,486
Is three days enough for Seoul?

197
00:07:29,486 --> 00:07:31,426
It covers the main palaces

198
00:07:31,426 --> 00:07:32,726
a traditional market

199
00:07:32,726 --> 00:07:34,506
a shopping street and a city view

200
00:07:34,506 --> 00:07:36,266
at a comfortable pace.

201
00:07:36,732 --> 00:07:39,732
Which day should you visit Gyeongbokgung?

202
00:07:39,732 --> 00:07:41,652
Any day except Tuesday

203
00:07:41,652 --> 00:07:43,392
when it's closed.

204
00:07:43,392 --> 00:07:45,592
Weekday mornings are the quietest.

205
00:07:45,990 --> 00:07:48,510
Do you need to book anything?

206
00:07:48,510 --> 00:07:51,290
Most of this plan needs no booking at all.

207
00:07:51,290 --> 00:07:54,070
The one exception is the Secret Garden tour at

208
00:07:54,070 --> 00:07:55,270
Changdeokgung

209
00:07:55,270 --> 00:07:57,790
which has limited places.

210
00:07:57,790 --> 00:07:59,870
Popular restaurants can also have queues at

211
00:07:59,870 --> 00:08:00,850
busy times.

212
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:03,000
So that's three days in Seoul.

213
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,640
Day one, palaces

214
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:07,700
hanok lanes and the stream.

215
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:08,400
Day two

216
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:09,800
a market breakfast

217
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:12,400
Myeongdong and the sunset from Namsan.

218
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:13,420
Day three

219
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:14,900
whatever you love most.

220
00:08:15,498 --> 00:08:16,492
The full plan

221
00:08:16,492 --> 00:08:18,260
with links for every stop

222
00:08:18,260 --> 00:08:19,641
is on Korea Plainly.

223
00:08:19,641 --> 00:08:21,740
The link is in the description.

224
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:22,789
If this helped

225
00:08:22,789 --> 00:08:24,447
subscribe for more plain

226
00:08:24,447 --> 00:08:26,159
practical guides to Korea.

227
00:08:26,159 --> 00:08:28,558
Have a wonderful trip to Seoul.

